  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MHPSS Gaza 2024 &#x2013; WHO MHPSS Technical Working Group Coordinator</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Unrest in the Palestinian Territories has been on the rise in in the last six months, particularly in Gaza. In Gaza, the humanitarian consequences have been devastating, exacerbating the impact of almost 14 years of an Israeli blockade, internal Palestinian political divisions and recurrent escalations. With the recent escalation of the 7th of October 2023, according to a World Health Organization (WHO) situation report (sitrep) dated 2nd of April 2023, there are 32,975 fatalities, of which 72% are children and women, 75,572 injured, and 1.7 million people are displaced, which is 75% of the total population. 10 out of 36 hospitals are partially functioning, 27 out of 89 primary health care (PHC) facilities are functional. 28 patients reportedly died of malnutrition. In northern Gaza 12.4%-16.5% of children form 6 to 59 months old are suffering from acute malnutrition. In southern Gaza 2-6% of children are suffering from acute malnutrition. There are ongoing outbreaks of diarrheal illnesses and hepatitis A.The Palestinian Ministry of Health (MOH) Mental Health department (MH) services are not functional. There used to be six community MH centres and one psychiatric hospital. Only one Community Mental Health Center (CMHC) in Rafah and two PHC centres are providing MH support and psychotropics. UNRWA and local non-governmental organizations (NGOS) such as the Gaza Community Mental Health Programme (GCMHP) are providing support in Rafah area too.</narrative>
  </description>
